course: dictionary
lesson: 10055
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. «Testament» has three meanings: a main part of the Bible, a clear proof of something, and a will.
explain: «Paul wrote letters to churches, such as Romans, Corinthians and Galatians, which are now part of the New Testament.» Letters, churches and Paul point to the Bible, so here testament means one of the main parts of the Bible.
explain: «The bridge is a testament to their hard work.» There is no Bible or law here. The bridge shows that people worked hard, so testament means clear proof of something. Check by swapping in the meaning: «The bridge is clear proof of their hard work» still makes sense.
fact: The Old Testament and the New Testament are the two main parts of the Christian Bible.
fact: The Old Testament has the Hebrew scriptures, and stories such as Noah, Moses and David.
fact: The New Testament tells of Jesus and the early Church.
fact: «A testament to something» means clear proof of it.
fact: In law, a testament is a will, as in «last will and testament».
exercise: «Christians read the Hebrew Bible as their Old Testament.» What is the Old Testament? | *One of the two main parts of the Christian Bible | Clear proof of hard work | A very old castle | A list of promises made to a friend
exercise: Noah, Moses and David are stories from which part of the Bible? | A last will and testament | The New Testament | A testament to hard work | *The Old Testament
exercise: «Her hard work is a testament to her skill.» What does testament mean here? | *Clear proof of something | A very old story | A part of the Bible about Jesus | A will left after someone dies
test: In «last will and testament», what does testament mean? | Part of the Bible | Clear proof of something | *A will, the paper saying who gets a person's things after they die | A very old map
test: «The Gospels are part of the New Testament.» Which part of the Bible tells of Jesus and the early Church? | *The New Testament | A testament to a bridge | The Old Testament | A last will and testament
exam: «The new school is a testament to the town's hard work and care.» What does testament mean? | A very old church | Part of the Bible about Moses | *Clear proof of the town's hard work and care | A will left by someone
